    "title": "The Culmination of Designing and Building with AI",
    "placeholder": "Enter your reflection here.",
    "long_instructions": "Throughout this professional learning module, you have explored the essential components and strategies needed to facilitate this project.\r\n\r\n## Workflow\r\n\r\nHow to guide students through:\r\n\r\n* Milestones to define evidence of learning  \r\n* Benchmarks to pause, review progress, and rotate the Project Leader role  \r\n\r\n## Tools\r\n\r\nHow to use:\r\n\r\n* The **Kanban Project Planning Board** to make daily work visible  \r\n* The **Capstone.md File** to capture the *how* and *why* behind decisions  \r\n\r\n## Grading Strategies\r\n\r\nHow to evaluate **holistic student growth** by:\r\n\r\n* Looking across multiple artifacts  \r\n* Valuing reasoning and clarity over feature count\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n    ➡️ Explore the full  <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-semester2-2025/units/6/lessons/1' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>lesson plan</a> here.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Reflection\r\n\r\n\r\n>In an era where AI tools can easily generate code or suggest features, this capstone requires us to assess student judgment rather than just their final product.\r\n>\r\n> Knowing that a polished app without clear reasoning may score lower than a simpler app with strong explanations and intentional scope, how will you shift your classroom culture so that students value clear reasoning, intentional trade-offs, and process over simply racing to finish the project?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
